From 0cea8c0084d43e10d2172c2933a4d8f36cff6b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:22:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [DS4.1] Engine grid: real rows from token ids

Base: candidate-57's vLLM tree d74e38eefbda (the 1107 series with
candidates 55-57); engine_grid, make_dummy and the DSpark drafter's
padding rows are as in candidate-58's tree.

Rationale:
A dummy batch's rows are token 0 and marked padding (make_dummy), and
the MoE routers give padding rows expert -1 (VLLM_MOE_SKIP_PADDING, on
by default), as the DSpark drafter does for its dummy query rows. So
every engine-grid step ran no routed expert at any shape: the grid
timed a decode step without its largest cost.

GPUModelRunner.engine_grid shapes may now carry token_ids (num_tokens
ids). Their dummy batches take those ids and mark their rows real, in
the target (InputBatch.make_dummy, via InputBuffers.dummy_input_ids) and
in the drafter's query (DFlashSpeculator.dummy_rows_live), so the
routers route them as they route text. Rows past the ids (a CUDA
graph's padding) stay token 0 and padding, as in serving. Each shape's
result reports real_rows, so a client can tell a server that ignored
the ids. Without token_ids nothing changes.

Quality:
Serving is unchanged: the ids are set only inside engine_grid (the
dev-mode collective RPC) and cleared after each dummy run. Graph
capture, the memory profile, the cost profile and every other dummy run
keep token 0 and padding rows.

Tests:
- tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_token_ids.py (new, CUDA): dummy
  batches take the ids as real rows, rows past them stay padding, and
  clearing the ids restores token 0 and padding.
- pytest tests/v1/worker/test_engine_grid_token_ids.py
  tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_input_batch_v2.py tests/v1/worker/test_dead_rows.py
  on spark-ds41f:candidate-57 with this commit mounted (sp8): 70 passed.
- spark-ds41f experiments/2026-11-10-grid-diverse-tokens: the routes
  census and the grid's step times with and without token ids.

Upstream status: local, for spark-ds41f's servebench engine grid
(version 2); engine_grid itself is a local patch (0139).
